1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,580
Most shop tools show a red bar. A red bar is not a reason. At Ajao
Precision Works in Lagos, Takt tells you why you're late, and what
would fix it.

2
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:19,330
High-mix shops in Lagos don't lose dates because one operation is
slow. Jobs wait behind a constrained work center, and that queue is
where the promise disappears.

3
00:00:19,710 --> 00:00:36,680
Takt opens on the diagnosis board. Lekki Fluid's adapter plate,
J-1051, is 26h 40m late. Every minute traces to queue time at
CNC-02, running at 91% load. Named. Measured. Causal.

4
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:49,970
Before Tunde buys another machine, test the fix. Add one machine at
CNC-02. Same seed, one capacity change. The late job clears, and all
1,600 lost minutes come back.

5
00:00:50,350 --> 00:01:01,010
The floor is real, too. Search the job book, filter by status, copy
the rows as CSV. No fake export buttons. No dead controls.

6
00:01:01,390 --> 00:01:10,580
Accounts are optional. A guest key opens the shop instantly. Sign
in, and every workspace stays separate, with its own people and
data.

7
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:24,980
Authority is enforced on the Serverpod API, not the interface. Tunde
owns. Ngozi edits. Amina reads, and the server rejects every write.
Hiding a button is UX. Rejecting the write is security.

8
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:34,650
Takt is Flutter and Serverpod, with real auth, real Postgres, 30
server tests, and 17 Flutter tests. The scheduler that tells you why
you're late.
